# Where `python -m cas12a.cnn_single` writes one run per `run_id` (#116).
#
# Same split as the rules above this directory: the evidence JSON is the
# reproducibility record and is small, so it stays tracked; the checkpoint is
# large and matters only once something decides to adopt it, at which point it
# goes under `models/` like every other adopted checkpoint. The repo's
# top-level `*.csv` rule already covers `validation_predictions.csv`, whose
# sha256 is recorded in the run's tracked `status.json`.
#
# This file lives here rather than in the root `.gitignore` so that the
# directory exists in a fresh checkout and a run never has to create it.
*.keras
